Z||000000||koolgtz||11-10-2001||02:04 AM||||whats up everyone. I'm new to this fourm but new to Fiero's. I've owned five over the years but my 1985 GT Is my baby and i had it for more than eight years. Having a family and a Beretta GTZ the Beretta sees alot more uuse than the Fiero. Lately I've been thinking of replacing the Fiero and the Beretta with a Subaru WRX but I changed my mine . I LOVE my GT and I couldn't do it.<BR>My project now is to drop in a HO Quad4 that I'm currently rebuilding. I want the dash to remain as stock as possible. To do this, I need to know from other members what did you change or had to buy to make theFiero speedo work with the Quad4 computer? ||||reg||12
Z||000001||fierojp||11-10-2001||02:47 AM||||This place has what you need.  Give them a call...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.dakotadigital.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dakotadigital.com/</A> <P>JP||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||11-10-2001||10:27 PM||||Nah, don't call Dakota Digital unless you've got deep pockets. Instead, head to Radio Shack with a dollar. Here's the circuit that I have used on a few 3800 and V8 conversions. Joe Wynman wrote the article, but he left out one important detail. You need to connect the purple wire from the speedo to ground or it will not work at all. If your speedometer reading is incorrect due to different tire size, then you'll need to call Dakota Digital or have your ECM reprogrammed.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/q4_spdo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||koolgtz||11-11-2001||02:08 PM||||Thanks for the info. I'll buy the parts today so that I could complete this technical part of my project. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||11-11-2001||03:26 PM||||Doing anything special for the rebuild?  w-41 cams or the like?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||koolgtz||11-13-2001||02:51 AM||||the quad4 is a 1990 out of a Beretta GTZ. I'm looking to get reasonable performance out of it. I've always liked the Quad4 ever since I got the GTZ. I did do the W41 cams as well as the W41 chip. The came gears are no longer available through GM but you could get them through Mantapart. I might do it but I don't know yet, at $125.00 they are not cheap. I'm keeping my rebuild/swap at a budget cause if you don't, these things have a way of getting out of hand.||||reg||6
